# Moment maps and line imaging products

Collapses a continuum-subtracted line cube into 2D maps: moment 0 (integrated intensity, Jy/beam km/s),
moment 1 (velocity), moment 2 (intensity-weighted velocity dispersion, sigma not FWHM), moment 8 or peak
brightness temperature. Every map depends on three choices: the **velocity window**, the **mask or clip**
and the **velocity estimator**. The two mistakes that matter most: (1) clipping moment 0 with a hard
per-pixel sigma cut and then quoting it as a total flux, which drops faint extended emission
(2013ApJ...769L..12L; several papers leave moment 0 unclipped or only signal-masked and clip only moments 1
and 2: 2020ApJ...903..145L, 2023A&A...677A..76P, 2024ApJ...964..190L), and (2) reading moment 2 as
intrinsic turbulence when it also contains beam smearing of rotation and multiple velocity components
(2019MNRAS.487..444R treats M2 only as an upper limit on intrinsic dispersion).

> Always report: velocity window (or mask recipe), clip threshold for each moment and what it is applied to
> (voxel, peak or integrated S/N), channel width, rms per channel and how it was measured, weighting,
> whether maps are primary-beam corrected, rest frequency, velocity frame and Doppler convention, the
> systemic velocity adopted, and the absolute flux-scale uncertainty. The cards flag moment-map clipping
> thresholds as not stated in 18 card entries (10 + 8 across two phrasings) and primary-beam correction
> details in 23 (16 + 7), pack aggregates; writing these down already beats a good share of the literature.

## When to use

- A detected line needs a morphology map, total flux, sizes or radial profile (2016A&A...592A..76D,
  2020A&A...644A..84M, 2021A&A...655A..80D, 2025A&A...703A..15M).
- A velocity field for a rotation or Keplerian fit, dynamical mass, PA or inclination (2020ApJ...891...48H,
  2018ApJ...868..113T, 2025ApJ...988...72S, 2020ApJ...890..167T, 2022A&A...662A.121R).
- Weak disk lines where a Keplerian mask raises S/N (2017A&A...606A.125S, 2018A&A...614A.106C, 2021ApJ...911..150P).
- Outflow lobe maps (2021A&A...648A..41V, 2019A&A...632A..33A); line-ratio maps on a common grid and mask
  (2024ApJ...971..176H, 2024ApJ...977...37N).
- Integrated-flux upper limits (2017AJ....153..240A, 2018ApJ...853..147M, 2024A&A...682A.166F), and input
  maps for lens models or source extraction (2018ApJ...867..140L, 2014A&A...568A..92M, 2024A&A...687A.163B).

## When not to use

| Situation | Use instead |
|---|---|
| Line has several velocity components, self-absorption or broad wings along the same sightline | Per-pixel multi-Gaussian fits (1-3 Gaussians with BIC selection in 2021ApJ...908..231M; iterative Gaussian adding in 2018ApJ...865...13T), or channel maps and PV diagrams (2015ApJ...815..106H) |
| Intrinsic velocity dispersion or rotation curve of a beam-smeared galaxy | Model the cube in 3D instead of reading moment 2 (3DBarolo named 19 times, 14 + 5 spellings, pack aggregates). 2021ApJ...908...19B fits the data cube directly with a beam-convolved thin-disk model whose intrinsic flux map comes from Richardson-Lucy deconvolution of the moment 0 map. 2021A&A...654A..37D found map-based velocity estimates about a factor of 2 below its modelled values. Note what one paper actually did: 2025ApJ...988...72S ran 3DBarolo on the moment-1 map with stellar PA, inclination, centre and vsys fixed, fitted a tanh rotation curve to its points and subtracted the model from moment 1 |
| Disk kinematics needing emission height, planet kinks or pressure bumps | Fitted peak velocity (bettermoments quadratic) plus eddy / disksurf fits (2024ApJ...974..102S, 2020ApJ...891...48H, 2024ApJ...964..190L) |
| Line flux of an unresolved or barely resolved source | An aperture spectrum with a Gaussian fit (2026A&A...705A..81K, 2024A&A...682A.166F) or a uv-plane fit are alternatives to integrating moment 0. Whichever you use, state and check the aperture, velocity window, noise estimate and recovered flux (2024A&A...682A.166F used a 0.7 arcsec aperture said to hold 99% of the flux and rechecked non-detections with other apertures and channel binning) |
| Clumpy or irregular sources | Aperture photometry on moment 0 rather than a 2D Gaussian, which fits these poorly (2024A&A...686A.156D) |
| Infall versus rotation in envelopes | PV diagrams along chosen PAs (2018PASJ...70...85T, 2015ApJ...815..106H) |
| Many weak transitions of one species, or a weak line with a detected partner | Stack transitions or spectra (inverse-variance stacking of moment maps in 2019ApJ...871..112X; Keplerian-shifted stacking in 2016ApJ...832..204Y), or a matched filter built from the detected line (HCO+ as the N2H+ template in 2024ApJ...972...88L) |

## Steps

1. **Start from a clean, continuum-subtracted cube.**
   - Continuum subtraction is the most common unstated setting (line-free channels or method flagged in about
     227 card entries across 13 phrasings, pack aggregates). Record the line-free ranges and fit order. In
     archival pipeline cubes the continuum channels come from a joint moment 0 / moment 8 mask (above 5 and
     4 times the MAD) that assumes about 19% of channels are line-free (2023PASP..135g4501H); check them
     against your line. STATCONT is "not optimal for spectral lines close to the noise level" (2021A&A...656A..46M).
   - Weighting: Briggs robust 0.5 is the most common stated choice (15 papers in my count of listed parameter
     lines, e.g. 2014ApJ...783L..13P, 2024ApJ...975...72B); robust 2 or natural is close behind for faint
     lines (18, e.g. 2018A&A...617A..23B, 2025ApJ...988...72S); robust 1.0 for 12CO and 2.0 for 13CO and C18O
     in 2020ApJ...889L..24P. 2018A&A...615A.155H made moment 0 at robust 0.0, moments 1-2 at robust 2.0.
   - Channel width: set by science. Disks 0.11-0.43 km/s (2024ApJ...972...88L, 2018ApJ...868..113T,
     2024ApJ...964..190L). Nearby galaxies a few to ~20 km/s (3.8 km/s in 2025ApJ...988...72S; 10.2 km/s in
     2019ApJ...881...10B for the NGC 3258 circumnuclear disk; 20 km/s in 2025MNRAS.537..520Z). Galactic Center
     circumnuclear disk 5 km/s (2018PASJ...70...85T). High-z 35-50 km/s (2020MNRAS.493.4294B 35 km/s at
     z = 8.31, 2019ApJ...881...63N 50 km/s at z = 7.5).
   - JvM correction: 2024ApJ...974..102S applied it (epsilon 0.71, 0.47, 0.33, 0.31 for 12CO, 13CO, C18O,
     H2CO) and confirmed results do not depend on it; 2024ApJ...964..190L applied it (0.61, 0.46) and warns it
     "can underestimate effective rms". It is not a rule tied to the number of configurations. General
     practice: apply it only when the restoring-beam and dirty-beam (residual) flux normalizations differ,
     derive epsilon for your own product, measure the rms on the corrected cube and say which you used.
   - Software (pack aggregates): CASA 467 mentions (tclean 40 + 6, uvcontsub 15), GILDAS 27, MIRIAD 17.
2. **Measure the noise per channel.** Use line-free channels or emission-free regions: emission-free regions
   matching the extraction aperture (2026A&A...705A..81K), 16-20 random off-source apertures
   (2022MNRAS.510.1148S, 2025A&A...703A..15M), 100 random background annuli (2022A&A...662A.121R), or images
   without the Keplerian mask (2024ApJ...975...72B). Make the mask on a flat-noise map and measure flux on the
   primary-beam-corrected map (2018ApJ...867..140L). Record the velocity metadata at the same time: rest frequency, frame (LSR velocities are the usual
   choice, e.g. 2018ApJ...869...59W; barycentric in 2020ApJ...892...99C), Doppler convention (radio,
   nu_obs = nu_rest (1 - V/c), in 2018ApJ...866..117C) and the systemic velocity reference. When you import
   mask or model geometry from another paper, check its conventions: 2019ApJ...873...73Z defines inclination
   with edge-on = 0, the opposite of the usual face-on = 0.
3. **Choose the velocity window.** Patterns in the pack (more in `references/parameters.md`):
   - Fixed window around systemic velocity: +/-7 km/s (2018ApJ...853..147M), +/-12 km/s (2014ApJ...791L...6W),
     300 km/s windows per lens component (2018ApJ...867..140L).
   - From a Gaussian fit to the spectrum: +/-2 sigma_V (2023MNRAS.519.2030H) to 3x FWHM (2020ApJ...903...34A).
     A narrower window loses flux: 2025A&A...694A.171M used peak +/-1.4 sigma (~83%) and a ~1.20 correction.
   - Window that maximises S/N: searched in an aperture (2024A&A...686A.156D); -140 to +140 km/s picked for
     the highest S/N and checked by eye (2020MNRAS.493.4294B). Channels with significant signal only:
     "contiguous channels above 2 sigma, peak above 3 sigma" (2025NatAs...9.1476C); >3 sigma channels summed
     (2019MNRAS.485..739M).
   - Broad window for complex-molecule maps, then a narrower one as a check (about 35 km/s in
     2024A&A...687A.163B; narrower gave consistent sizes and positions).
   - Contamination: narrow the window to avoid a neighbouring line (2024A&A...688A.130H) or outflow wings
     (2020MNRAS.496.2790L). Blends: from -5 km/s of the lowest to +5 km/s of the highest line (2018ApJ...857...35S).
   - Outflow lobes: separate blue and red ranges, excluding cloud-velocity channels (2021A&A...648A..41V;
     blue -400 to -120 and red +120 to 300 km/s in 2019A&A...632A..33A).
4. **Build the mask.** Pick one recipe and state its parameters, including whose rms the threshold uses
   (2026ApJ..1005...94N quotes 0.5 sigma of the unsmoothed cube as 8 sigma of the smoothed one).

   | Recipe | Parameters seen | Papers |
   |---|---|---|
   | Per-pixel sigma clip (`includepix` in immoments, `-clip` in bettermoments) | moment 0: 3 sigma; moments 1-2: 4 sigma | 2016A&A...590A..73A, 2020A&A...640A.104A, 2025A&A...699A..83A |
   | Smooth-and-mask (mask from smoothed cube, moments on unsmoothed cube) | spatial 1-3 beams, most often 1.5x beam; spectral Hanning, boxcar 4 channels, factor 4, or unstated; threshold 0.5-3 sigma | 2018ApJ...865...13T (beam FWHM, 1.5 sigma, spectral kernel unstated), 2021MNRAS.500.3802H (1.5x, 4x, 3 sigma), 2022MNRAS.512.1522D (1.5x beam, 4-channel boxcar, 3 rms), 2026MNRAS.546f2269R (1.5x beam, Hanning, 0.9 sigma), 2025MNRAS.541.2540Z (3x beam, Hanning over 5 channels, 1 sigma) |
   | Seed and grow (PHANGS style) | seed 3.5-5 sigma in 2-3 consecutive channels, grow to 1.5-3 sigma | 2024ApJ...971..176H (5 to 2, two channels each), 2023A&A...671A...3J (3.5 in 3 channels, 2 in 2), 2019ApJ...876..141I (5 to 1.5), 2025ApJ...988..162D (4 to 2, +10 km/s), 2023ApJ...945...42B (5 to 3, regions under a beam area removed) |
   | Contiguous-channel mask (MASKMOMENT) | >3 sigma in 2 contiguous channels | 2025ApJ...988...72S |
   | 3DBarolo SEARCH / smooth and search | SNRCUT 3.5-4.5, GROWTHCUT 2-4.5, MINCHANNELS 2-3 | 2025A&A...693A..91L, 2025PASJ...77..432U, 2022NatCo..13.4574G |
   | Source finder (SoFiA, 6 in aggregates) | 4 sigma on several smoothed cubes; merge 2 px / 3 chan; integrated S/N > 3 | 2019PASJ...71...85M |
   | MAD-based per spaxel | channels above ~5 MAD | 2021A&A...654A..24B, 2026A&A...706A.236M |
   | Morphological cleanup | fill holes < 2 beams; drop islands < 1 beam | 2024MNRAS.527.9343L |
   | Keplerian mask (disks; keplerian_mask named 5 times) | M*, PA, i, centre from literature; vsys and line width tuned for S/N | 2017A&A...606A.125S, 2018A&A...614A.106C, 2020ApJ...890..142P, 2021ApJ...911..150P, 2024ApJ...964..190L |

   - For line ratios, build one combined mask over all lines (2024ApJ...971..176H "combo" mask) and use the
     same velocity range for every map (2024ApJ...977...37N).
   - Keplerian masks: pad them for flared emitting layers (2019ApJ...876...72L) or enlarge the outer radius
     (1.5x in 2025ApJ...989....3D), and check the mask covers all the emission (2018ApJ...868..113T).
     2017A&A...606A.125S reports an S/N gain of about 2. Line-width parameters r0 = 100 au, q = -0.3,
     v0 = 0.3 km/s (2020ApJ...890..142P) and V0 = 0.22-0.25 km/s, R0 = 100 AU, q = 0.3 (2021ApJ...911..150P)
     are two published sets; check how each paper writes the law and the sign of q before reusing either.
   - Velocity-matched extraction does the same for a ring: per pixel, sum only the channels at the expected
     Keplerian velocity (2015MNRAS.447.3936M).
5. **Compute the moments.**
   - Moment 0: sum over masked channels times channel width. CASA `immoments` (64 mentions, 37 + 27
     spellings, pack aggregates; e.g. 2020MNRAS.493.4294B, 2026A&A...707A.120H). For flux, prefer an
     unclipped or signal-masked map over a hard per-pixel clip (2020ApJ...903..145L leaves moment 0
     unclipped; 2023A&A...677A..76P uses no sigma clip in immoments; 2024ApJ...964..190L masks without a flux
     threshold). Clipping only negative values (`includepix` from 0) also biases a noisy sum high (general
     practice); papers do it where absorption overlaps the line (2024MNRAS.533..771R) or without saying why
     (2025ApJ...988..106H, 2024A&A...692A.155K), so say so if you do.
   - Velocity: intensity-weighted moment 1 is the default. The quadratic fit to the peak channel and its two
     neighbours (bettermoments) is used in the protoplanetary-disk examples here (2020ApJ...891...48H,
     2018ApJ...868..113T, 2024ApJ...974..102S, 2022A&A...662A.121R), in debris disks (2026A&A...705A.198M)
     and also outside disks (2024ApJ...963....1O, a cool-core cluster). bettermoments is named in 65
     matched steps (pack aggregates); that is a software count, not a count of papers using the quadratic
     estimator, so it does not show a majority. Gaussian fits per pixel are the other option
     (2018ApJ...853..147M; 2021ApJ...908..231M with 300 Monte Carlo iterations for errors).
     2024ApJ...974..102S compared moment 1, Gaussian and quadratic maps.
   - Velocity-map thresholds (29 papers in my count, listed in `references/parameters.md`): 4 sigma is the
     most common (8, e.g. 2022A&A...662A.121R, 2025ApJ...988..106H), then 3 sigma (6) and 5 sigma (3, e.g.
     2018A&A...615A.155H); the range runs from 1.5x local rms (2025Natur.641.1137B) to integrated S/N > 10
     (2021ApJ...917...99Y). The meaning is often not stated. Three kinds appear: a per-voxel clip before
     collapsing (2014ApJ...788L..34P), a blank on the pixel's spectral peak (2026A&A...705A.198M at 3.5 sigma,
     2026MNRAS.552g1700S at 3 sigma), and a blank on moment-0 S/N (2021A&A...653A.111R, 2023MNRAS.518.3183L).
     2024ApJ...963....1O clips "all pixels with S/N < 3.5 sigma"; most others give a number only. Say which.
   - Moment 8 (peak intensity) maps per transition: 2019ApJ...871..112X made them only from transitions it
     selected as uncontaminated, stacked them, and still could not fix the AcA morphology because of spatial
     contamination. Before assigning a peak map to a species, confirm its velocity interval is free of other
     lines or decompose the spectrum. Peak brightness temperature through the full Planck function from
     bettermoments quadratic peaks is used in 2026A&A...705A.198M and 2024ApJ...964..190L.
   - Moment 2: the intensity-weighted velocity dispersion (sigma). For a Gaussian, FWHM = 2.355 sigma; keep the
     two apart when comparing with fitted widths (2018ApJ...865...13T quotes FWHM 342 km/s and sigma 145 km/s
     for one component). Channel width and the spectral response also broaden it; the cards rarely state a
     correction (2014ApJ...794L..10Y corrected narrow widths for its 0.60 km/s resolution). Treat it as an
     upper limit on intrinsic dispersion where rotation is unresolved (2019MNRAS.487..444R) and compare it
     only at matched resolution (2025A&A...699A..83A blames higher CO(3-2) dispersions partly on the coarser
     beam). A noise-robust alternative is the effective width sigma_v = I / (sqrt(2 pi) T_peak), equal to
     moment 2 for a Gaussian profile (2024ApJ...971..176H, which Nyquist-samples the maps).
6. **Attach uncertainties and limits.**
   - Per beam, for a moment 0 (Jy/beam km/s) summed over N channels of width dv with per-channel rms sigma:
     sigma_mom0 = sigma * dv * sqrt(N), with N all channels in the window (2024ApJ...977...37N states this
     form). With correlated channels (Hanning smoothing, oversampled channels) use dv * sqrt(sum_ij C_ij),
     where C is the channel covariance; the sqrt(N) form then underestimates the noise (general practice).
   - Aperture flux (general practice): summing a Jy/beam km/s map over N_pix pixels gives Jy km/s only after
     multiplying by Omega_pix / Omega_beam, and since pixels within a beam are correlated the noise scales with
     the number of beams, about sigma_mom0 * sqrt(N_pix * Omega_pix / Omega_beam), not sigma_mom0 * sqrt(N_pix).
     Papers do this (sqrt of the beams in the region: 2024A&A...690A.255D, 2020MNRAS.499.5136C) or, better,
     use blank apertures of the same size and window (2026A&A...705A..81K, 2025A&A...703A..15M). The
     sigma_rms sqrt(npts) (pixel scale)^2 of 2019PASJ...71...85M is for their molecular-mass noise map, not
     a recipe for Jy/beam maps.
   - Calibration: report statistical and absolute flux-scale errors separately (2014ApJ...790..160S
     +/-0.07 (rms) +/-0.07 (calibration) mJy; 15% in 2018PASJ...70...85T; 5% Band 3 and 10% Band 6 in
     2025ApJ...995..108J). 2021A&A...656A..46M, 2020ApJ...892...99C and 2024A&A...686A.156D (up to 10%) say
     their errors exclude it; cards flag it as not stated in about 50 entries (18 + 16 + 9 + 7, pack
     aggregates). Add continuum-subtraction and fixed-parameter systematics where they matter.
   - Upper limits, general form: k * dv * sqrt(sum_ij C_ij) over the assumed line width, with k the stated
     significance (3 in 9 papers in my count; galaxy examples assume 100-320 km/s widths, e.g.
     2021A&A...655A..42S, 2024ApJ...964...95S). State k, the assumed width, the extraction region and how
     the noise was measured. Paper recipes are paper-specific, not portable defaults (details and caveats in
     `references/parameters.md`): 2017AJ....153..240A used 3x image rms over +/-1 km/s of the stellar
     velocity; 2018ApJ...853..147M's CO-shifted, CO-masked 3 sigma limits (rms times the number of
     independent channels across the CO width) assume every molecule shares CO's spectro-spatial
     distribution, so they checked the filter on CO and also gave unfiltered limits within +/-5 km/s; in
     2024A&A...682A.166F (Gaussian, FWHM 600 km/s) "1 sigma" is the assumed peak amplitude, not the confidence
     level, and non-detections were rechecked with other apertures and binning; 2024A&A...691A.178B gives only
     a detection threshold (non-detection if S/N < 3).
   - Position uncertainty: about beam / (S/N) (2016A&A...592A..76D; beam major axis and S/N in
     2023MNRAS.519.2030H).
7. **Measure derived quantities.** Sizes and PAs from 2D Gaussian fits, the most common fitting phrase in
   the aggregates (2D Gaussian 11, plus variants): CASA `imfit` on averaged, normalised moment-0 maps in
   2020A&A...644A..84M; a 2D Gaussian fit to the moment-0 map for the PA in 2014ApJ...784...78R (software
   not named). `imfit` is named 51 times (imfit 27 + casa imfit 24, pack aggregates). Alternatives:
   curve-of-growth photometry in elliptical annuli (2022A&A...662A.121R, 2025A&A...703A..15M), or a size
   from the area above half the line peak, theta_S = sqrt(theta_50^2 - theta_beam^2) (2024MNRAS.533.1143M).
   Radial profiles from azimuthal averaging (gofish, 20 mentions, pack aggregates; 1/4-beam bins and a
   30 deg wedge along the major axis in 2021ApJS..257....6G). 2021A&A...655A..80D made such profiles and,
   separately, measured extents from the 2 sigma moment-0 contours, binning contour values with at least 10
   samples per bin (angular ranges >= 60 deg). Velocity gradients from a plane fit to moment 1
   (2024ApJ...977...37N). Gas masses go to the gas-mass skill (examples: alpha_CO 4.3 with R21 0.8 in
   2025ApJ...988...72S; X_CO 2e20 in 2019PASJ...71...85M).
8. **Fit the velocity field (optional).** eddy (12 mentions) for disks, 3DBarolo (19) and kinemetry (5)
   for galaxies, emcee (17), pack aggregates. Free parameters are usually centre, PA, inclination, vsys
   (2018ApJ...864..133T, 2018ApJ...869L..50P, 2022A&A...662A.121R); fix PA and inclination from continuum
   when the line is noisier (2020ApJ...891...48H, 2024ApJ...974..102S). Exclude the inner beam: fit radii
   start at 1.5x beam major axis in 2024ApJ...974..102S. Fix M* and distance but repeat the fit at
   M* +/- 1 sigma (2022A&A...662A.121R). 3DBarolo ring widths: the beam minor-axis FWHM
   (2022NatCo..13.4574G), minor-axis FWHM / 2.5 (2021A&A...654A..37D) or major-axis FWHM / 2.5
   (2026A&A...707A.252K). A second, independent fitter is a cheap check (DISCFIT against 3DBarolo in
   2024A&A...691A.118K, which notes that 3DBarolo's axisymmetric circular orbits miss a one-armed spiral and
   bias the inclination).

## Parameter defaults and ranges

Counts marked "my count" are from the pack's listed key-parameter lines (the pack lists the first part and
truncates the rest), so they are lower bounds. Longer per-paper lists: `references/parameters.md`.

| Parameter | Common choice | Range seen | Papers (count) | Examples |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Weighting for cubes | Briggs 0.5 | -2 to 2, natural | 15 robust 0.5; 18 robust 2 or natural (my count) | 2014ApJ...783L..13P, 2019A&A...621A..83S (-2 and 2), 2018Sci...362.1034D (2) |
| Moment 0 clip | none, a signal mask, or 3 sigma | 0 (negatives only) to 5 sigma | ~15 (my count) | 2016A&A...590A..73A (3), 2017ApJ...840...60B (5), 2026MNRAS.551g1645K (5), 2026MNRAS.552g1700S (1), 2023A&A...677A..76P (none) |
| Moment 1/2 threshold | 4 sigma, then 3 sigma | 1.5x local rms to 5 sigma; integrated S/N up to 10; voxel vs peak vs moment-0 S/N usually unstated | 29 (my count) | 2022A&A...662A.121R (4), 2021A&A...653A.111R (3 on moment-0 rms), 2026A&A...705A.198M (3.5 peak) |
| Smoothing for mask | 1.5x beam spatial | 1-3 beams; spectral as stated: Hanning (2019MNRAS.484.4239R, 2025MNRAS.541.2540Z, 2026MNRAS.546f2269R), 4-channel boxcar (2022MNRAS.512.1522D), factor 4 (2021MNRAS.500.3802H), two-channel smoothing with kernel not named (2020A&A...640A.104A), width unstated (2018ApJ...865...13T) | 7 | as listed |
