# Codex refresh review: moment-maps
VERDICT: FIX
REFRESH: PARTIAL

## Findings

- RR-01 | medium | stale | “Channel width … 0.11 … to 50 km/s” | The rebuilt pack includes 100 km/s channels in 2021ApJ...921...97J and 2022PASJ...74.1429T, and disk channels of 1.6 km/s in 2025A&A...703A..15M. | Update the table and Step 1 ranges, or explicitly label them as selected examples.
- RR-02 | medium | broken-edit | “Velocity-map … thresholds, 29 papers” | The supplied reference table enumerates 28 unique bibcodes. It also omits explicit rebuilt-pack cases such as 2026A&A...705A.201B: “peak emission above 4 sigma” and 2020MNRAS.496..138B: “SNR > 4 pixel cut.” | Rebuild the enumeration and synchronize its heading, counts and frequency claims throughout.
- RR-03 | medium | attribution | “moment 0: 3 sigma; moments 1–2: 4 sigma” | The mask-recipe row includes 2025A&A...699A..83A, whose excerpt says all its moment maps use “3σrms clipping.” | Assign thresholds paper by paper; identify this example as 3 sigma for moments 0–2.
- RR-04 | medium | attribution | “MAD-based per spaxel … channels above ~5 MAD” | 2026A&A...706A.236M instead specifies a significant **moment-0** detection above five MAD, followed by regional extraction. This is not a per-channel mask like the cited 2021A&A...654A..24B example. | Separate integrated-map detection from per-spaxel channel selection.
- RR-05 | medium | attribution | “300 Monte Carlo iterations”; “about 97%” flux recovery | Neither value is evidenced for 2021ApJ...908..231M in the supplied rebuild; its visible key-parameter entry gives initial width 20 km/s, maximum 500 km/s and an S/N ≥3 mask. | Supply the supporting excerpts or remove these numerical details; their absence does not establish that they are false.
- RR-06 | medium | unsupported | “robust 0.5 is the most common … 15”; “close behind … 18” | The truncated key-parameter listing cannot establish a corpus-wide mode. The wording also ranks the pooled 18 robust-2/natural examples behind 15 robust-0.5 examples. | Present these as explicitly enumerated subset counts and remove the ranking unless supported by complete, consistently grouped counts.
- RR-07 | medium | science | “sigma_v = I / (sqrt(2 pi) T_peak)” | The skill introduces integrated intensity in Jy/beam km/s but uses peak temperature here. The pack’s 2024ApJ...971..176H definition requires compatible integrated and peak intensity units to yield velocity. | Specify I in K km/s with T_peak in K, or use integrated and peak flux densities in matching units.
- RR-08 | medium | omission | “Start from a … continuum-subtracted cube” | This blanket instruction conflicts with the temperature workflow in 2024ApJ...964..190L, step 7: unsubtracted cubes are used to avoid underestimating intensity toward strong continuum. | Add a separate branch retaining and checking unsubtracted cubes for peak-brightness thermometry.
- RR-09 | medium | omission | “Thick lines … trace temperature” | The pack explicitly conditions this interpretation on LTE and beam filling in 2024ApJ...964..190L, step 7; it also warns that inner lines can become optically thin. | Require optical-depth, excitation and beam-filling checks before interpreting brightness temperature as gas temperature.
- RR-10 | medium | omission | “For line ratios, build one combined mask … same velocity range” | Matching masks and windows does not address differing spatial responses. The pack records a common 2″ beam and 10 kλ uv cutoff in 2022ApJ...929..100K, and warns about beam-size differences in 2024ApJ...977...37N. | Require common angular resolution, aligned grids and comparable spatial filtering before quantitative ratios.
- RR-11 | medium | omission | “Moment 2 is not turbulence” | The warning omits thermal broadening and unresolved hyperfine structure. The pack’s 2024ApJ...977...37N step 5 subtracts thermal and bulk contributions; 2026A&A...709A.173M treats widths as upper limits because hyperfine splitting was neglected. | Add both contributions to the width-interpretation checks before deriving turbulent dispersion.
- RR-12 | medium | omission | “Choose the velocity window” | No check establishes that the cube actually covers the line and wings. The pack reports entirely/partially missed lines in 2021A&A...654A..37D and truncated 13CO profiles for seven objects in 2026A&A...710A.390O. | Check usable spectral coverage before integration or fitting; flag truncated fluxes and widths.
- RR-13 | medium | omission | “Sizes and PAs from 2D Gaussian fits … theta_S = sqrt(…)” | The workflow lacks a resolved-size significance check. The pack’s 2024MNRAS.533.1143M explicitly prohibits morphological conclusions for unresolved emission; 2021ApJ...914...36I adopts a size upper limit for a 1.7-sigma extent. | Define theta_50, propagate size uncertainties and report unresolved or insignificant extents as limits.
- RR-14 | low | length | The main skill exceeds ~300 lines | Repeated software counts and extensive per-paper settings obscure the operational workflow. | Move software tallies, sampler settings and longer weighting, smoothing and window examples to `references/parameters.md`.

## Notes

The description’s 1087 papers and the software aggregate totals match the rebuilt pack.
No confirmed reversal of an item marked FIXED in the reconciliation was identified.
Historical reconciliation numbers should not replace the rebuilt aggregates.
